🚀 The feature, motivation and pitch
We are used to add custom symbolic follow this test:



      pytorch/test/onnx/test_custom_ops.py


        Lines 66 to 75
      in
      6f4dea5







           class MyClip(torch.autograd.Function): 




               @staticmethod 




               def forward(ctx, input, scalar): 




                   ctx.save_for_backward(input) 




                   return input.clamp(min=scalar) 









               @staticmethod 




               def symbolic(g, input, scalar): 




                   return g.op("Clip", input, min_f=scalar) 










When I turn to PyTorch >=1.13, export such custom op would give me logs:
FutureWarning: 'torch.onnx._patch_torch._graph_op' is deprecated in version 1.13 and will
 be removed in 1.14. Please note 'g.op()' is to be removed from torch.Graph.

Did that means symbolic in the autograd.Function would be deprecated? Or will the graph be wrapped into a GraphContext?
Besides, error happened when I am trying to export op below:
class CustomAdd(torch.autograd.Function):

    @staticmethod
    def forward(ctx, x, y):
        return x + 0

    @staticmethod
    def symbolic(g, x, y):
        return g.op('domain::CustomAdd', x, y)
with log:
    _C._jit_pass_peephole(graph, True)
IndexError: Argument passed to at() was not in the map.

It seems that ONNXAutogradFunctionProcess would trace the forward and inline it into the graph. Is it passible to disable the pass on special op?
forward might throw RuntimeError: _Map_base::at when we use torch.LongTensor or torch.arange, I have no idea about how to bypass it.
